WEBVTT

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the sixteenth. Can you all hear me? Right, let's get going.</v>

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:18.940
<v Grace Liu>Morning. Anyone actually manage their weekend plans with that weather? We planned a walk and got as far as the café.</v>

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:25.489
<v Jamie Brennan>That's a successful walk in my book. Mine involved a leaking shed and some fairly strong language.</v>

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:30.640
<v Aisha Begum>Did anyone watch the football last night, though? Honestly, those last ten minutes.</v>

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.890
<v Callum Reid>Don't. I've come to work to get away from that.</v>

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha, right. Before we get onto what's outstanding, anything finished off?</v>

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.649
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, tested the boiler safety valve yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done, nothing further from that test.</v>

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that's closed then.</v>

00:00:52.829 --> 00:01:00.530
<v Aisha Begum>And I finished the repair on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit last night. That's completed, not something still waiting for today.</v>

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.170
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. That one had been hanging about a bit.</v>

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:13.409
<v Hannah Price>Also, just because it was still showing in the old notes, I signed off the inspection on the fire alarm panel on Tuesday. Already done.</v>

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.530
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I've seen the sign-off. No outstanding action on that.</v>

00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:25.760
<v Callum Reid>Less cheerful one: still waiting on parts for the water booster. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.730
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, still waiting. No change on that, unfortunately.</v>

00:01:32.319 --> 00:01:41.069
<v Sarah Okafor>And we can't get to the palletiser until production gives us a window. That's still a blocker, not permission to dive in while it's running.</v>

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:46.909
<v Callum Reid>Absolutely. No one's going into it without the proper stop and isolation.</v>

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:56.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer by Wednesday? That's the job we need agreed, with that access constraint understood.</v>

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:09.099
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer by Wednesday, provided we get that production window. I can own it; I can't magic the access.</v>

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:14.969
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. By Wednesday remains the requirement, and the access blocker stays visible against it.</v>

00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:23.120
<v Aisha Begum>Um, while we're on noises and stoppages, I heard a slight rattle from the GT2. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, not turning that rattle into another job.</v>

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:36.729
<v David Whitfield>Same sort of thing from me: heard a slight rattle from the feedwater pump. Nothing to action yet on that either.</v>

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:43.830
<v Sarah Okafor>Separate from the noise, Dave, can you inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks tomorrow? No rush.</v>

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:49.330
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks tomorrow. No rush, understood.</v>

00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:55.900
<v Hannah Price>Just checking, that's a leak inspection, not a strip-down because of the rattle?</v>

00:02:57.919 --> 00:03:03.169
<v David Whitfield>Correct. Leaks only for that job. The slight rattle's just an observation at this point.</v>

00:03:05.009 --> 00:03:12.360
<v David Whitfield>And I'll investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 water valve tomorrow. That's a separate issue from the noise Aisha mentioned.</v>

00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:18.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, David Whitfield. Got you down for investigating the pressure drop on the GT2 water valve tomorrow.</v>

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:25.680
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, separate things. My rattle comment wasn't a request to start chasing that as well.</v>

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:33.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you book a contractor to look at the GT2? Monday for the booking, low priority.</v>

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:41.150
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll book a contractor to look at the GT2 on Monday, today. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:03:43.259 --> 00:03:48.860
<v Sarah Okafor>That's the booking on Monday, to be clear. We're not promising they'll actually be here today.</v>

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:53.240
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly, booking only. No attendance date being agreed here.</v>

00:03:54.620 --> 00:04:01.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you order spare parts for the trucks by 11am? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:10.240
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll order spare parts for the trucks by 11am. Not an emergency, but I won't let it slip.</v>

00:04:11.509 --> 00:04:14.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Welcome to the glamorous world of ordering things.</v>

00:04:15.669 --> 00:04:18.819
<v Aisha Begum>Living the dream. Almost as exciting as that football.</v>

00:04:19.279 --> 00:04:27.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, my bit: I'll update the risk assessment for work on the IM2 after lunch. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:04:28.819 --> 00:04:33.019
<v Grace Liu>So first after lunch, rather than it getting buried under everything else?</v>

00:04:34.769 --> 00:04:39.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. After lunch, that comes first for me because it's holding production up.</v>

00:04:41.439 --> 00:04:43.540
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Sarah. Clear on that one.</v>

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:54.199
<v Callum Reid>And I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team for next Tuesday. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Callum Reid. Toolbox talk for next Tuesday, then.</v>

00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:06.009
<v Callum Reid>Yep, I'll organise it. It's not a drop-everything one, but next Tuesday won't get forgotten.</v>

00:05:06.879 --> 00:05:11.779
<v Grace Liu>Good. Better than everyone discovering there's a talk as they're halfway through a brew.</v>

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:23.769
<v Sarah Okafor>We've also got the filter to swap on the Compressed Air Dryer, tomorrow at 9:30. That's holding production up so it needs doing first. Who can take that?</v>

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:28.730
<v David Whitfield>Um, I can't commit to that slot. Don't put my name against it.</v>

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:34.699
<v Callum Reid>I can't take it either. Sorry, talking over you there.</v>

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:43.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. The filter swap on the Compressed Air Dryer is still needed tomorrow at 9:30, but there's nobody owning it.</v>

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:47.519
<v Hannah Price>That's a fairly uncomfortable gap if it's holding production.</v>

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:54.689
<v Sarah Okafor>It is. The priority hasn't changed—it needs doing first—but I haven't got an acceptance, so it stays unassigned.</v>

00:05:55.689 --> 00:06:05.839
<v Grace Liu>There's another gap: someone needs to do a site visit at Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor today at 2pm. Fairly important, that one. I'm raising it, not volunteering.</v>

00:06:07.519 --> 00:06:12.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take the Harbour Road Warehouse visit with the contractor, today at 2pm?</v>

00:06:13.329 --> 00:06:19.980
<v Jamie Brennan>Not me, I'm afraid. And just to avoid crossed wires, accepting the GT2 booking wasn't me accepting this visit.</v>

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:23.800
<v Aisha Begum>I can't take the visit either.</v>

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:32.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Nobody assigned to the Harbour Road Warehouse visit. Today at 2pm is still the requirement; we're not pretending it's covered.</v>

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:37.420
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, fairly important still, even with that blank against it.</v>

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:45.189
<v Hannah Price>Nothing else from quality. The two things I mentioned were both finished, not additions to today's list.</v>

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And the observations haven't quietly become extra jobs either.</v>

00:06:50.449 --> 00:06:55.000
<v Jamie Brennan>Have we got an echo, or is someone agreeing with everything I say?</v>

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:01.199
<v David Whitfield>Definitely an echo. Don't get used to that level of support.</v>

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:08.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before Teams starts repeating the whole meeting, anything else already on the list that we've misunderstood?</v>

00:07:09.939 --> 00:07:11.139
<v Aisha Begum>No, clear here.</v>

00:07:11.839 --> 00:07:16.740
<v Callum Reid>Clear. Water booster's still blocked on parts, that's all—not another job I'm starting today.</v>

00:07:17.769 --> 00:07:20.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Thanks, everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>
